From 8b421ade00477ad7a60ecf1bb4376e221604e53c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:46:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove intrusive navToggle hamburger button from gallery
 pages

The button was unstyled (no CSS existed for #navToggle/.nav-toggle),
so it rendered with default browser button chrome on both mobile and
desktop, appearing as an unexplained white icon over the site.

- Removed the <button id="navToggle"> element from all 16 generated
  gallery pages
- Removed its emitting line from renderGalleryPage() in templates.js
  so it won't reappear on the next build
- Removed the now-dead click handler and related comment from
  scripts/site.js
